  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Calculating Mass from Linear Density</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Consider a thin rod  oriented on the \(x\)-axis  over the interval  \(\displaystyle  \left[{@a@}, {@b@}\right]\).</p>
<p>If the density of the road is given by \(\rho(x)={@rho_x@}\), what is the mass of the rod?</p><p>\(m =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]] </p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>To find the mass of the thin rod oriented on the \(x\)-axis over the interval  \(\displaystyle  \left[{@a@}, {@b@}\right]\) with a density function \(\rho(x) = {@rho_x@}\), you can use the following integral:</p>

<p>\(\displaystyle m = \int_{a}^{b} \rho(x) \, dx\)</p>

<p>In this case, \(\displaystyle \rho(x) = {@rho_x@}\), and the interval is \(\displaystyle  \left[{@a@}, {@b@}\right]\) , so the mass of the rod is:</p>

<p>\[\displaystyle 
\begin{align*}
m &= \int_{{@a@}}^{{@b@}} {@rho_x@} \, dx \\
    &=\big[ {@int(rho_x,x)@} \big]_{{@a@}}^{{@b@}}  \\
    &= {@mass@} \\
\end{align*}\]</p>
<p>So, the mass of the thin rod over the interval \(\displaystyle  \left[{@a@}, {@b@}\right]\) with a density function \(\rho(x) = {@rho_x@}\) is {@mass@} unit of mass.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
